    "synthesis": {
      "model_calls": 1,
      "phase": "synthesis",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Research an isolated path-search optimization: preserve the current spanning-tree edge order and branch order, but reduce repeated work in `buscaAresta`/`deep`. The existing CSR, shared-path and incremental-color changes were bundled and measured slower, so do not repeat that bundle unchanged. Try one component at a time and, if materializing adjacency, measure whether an empirically justified size threshold avoids setup overhead on small inputs. Preserve simple-path rules, first-success/best-so-far behavior, tie ordering and output formatting.",
        "B": "Focus on `Prim_ST`, which is repeatedly called during partition generation and rebuilds matrix state. Test reducing per-call matrix/allocation work—for example, apply excluded-edge checks logically over the existing graph and reuse scratch arrays—while preserving inclusion/exclusion constraints, root choice and minimum-key tie behavior. Keep this separate from changes to path search. The const-reference/min-selection and SIMD variants regressed; removing cycle checks alone also regressed, so do not assume either change or their combination helps. Verify correctness before timing.",
        "C": "Investigate the partition worklist independently. `create_partitions` always selects the final element of `partitions` by scanning to it and erasing it; test replacing that with `back()`/`pop_back()` to retain the same LIFO order while avoiding the scan and vector shift. Measure this simple change before trying to reduce partition copies. Preserve child-generation order and Prim constraints, and test cases that create many partitions as well as small cases.",
        "G": "Use the correct baseline (mean 0.006293 s) as the comparison point. None of the currently measured admissible transformations beat it: means range from 0.007796 s to 0.010386 s, including the cycle-check removal, const-reference/min-selection, CSR/path-search, and SIMD experiments. Do not import those changes merely because their individual operations look cheaper. Integrate only complete child candidates with correctness evidence; measure each integrated program and relevant combinations as whole binaries, since interaction gains are not additive. Retain the baseline if no correct combination is faster. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions or source outside the candidate integration.",
        "analysis": "The official task requires a valid path with as many distinct colors as possible; the source also imposes observable traversal and tie ordering through spanning-tree generation and recursive search. Optimization work should therefore preserve path validity, color counting, and reference-compatible output behavior for general valid inputs, not target the observed cases. The baseline passed all four measured cases. Its mean was 0.0062925 s; every supplied transformed program was slower: cycle-check removal 0.007796 s, parallel min selection 0.008244 s, B's reference/flag/path changes 0.008256 s, A's CSR/search changes 0.009299 s, SIMD min scan 0.009937 s, and flattened matrices 0.010386 s. These results counsel isolating changes, accounting for setup overhead, and measuring integration rather than inferring gains from source-level operation counts."
      },
